  ],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Counting is already a good solution.",
      "start_ms": 0,
      "end_ms": 2120,
      "start_frame": 0,
      "end_frame": 64,
      "word_count": 6
    },
    {
      "text": "It runs in linear time, and it uses only constant extra space.",
      "start_ms": 2640,
      "end_ms": 7560,
      "start_frame": 79,
      "end_frame": 227,
      "word_count": 12
    },
    {
      "text": "So what is still missing?",
      "start_ms": 8100,
      "end_ms": 9260,
      "start_frame": 243,
      "end_frame": 278,
      "word_count": 5
    },
    {
      "text": "The follow -up asks for one pass, but counting needs two separate passes.",
      "start_ms": 10160,
      "end_ms": 15260,
      "start_frame": 305,
      "end_frame": 458,
      "word_count": 13
    },
    {
      "text": "In the first pass, we only learn the frequencies.",
      "start_ms": 15940,
      "end_ms": 19020,
      "start_frame": 478,
      "end_frame": 571,
      "word_count": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "How many zeros, how many ones, and how many twos.",
      "start_ms": 19720,
      "end_ms": 24000,
      "start_frame": 592,
      "end_frame": 720,
      "word_count": 10
    },
    {
      "text": "At that point, the array is still not arranged.",
      "start_ms": 24680,
      "end_ms": 27840,
      "start_frame": 740,
      "end_frame": 835,
      "word_count": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "Then we need another pass.",
      "start_ms": 28180,
      "end_ms": 29700,
      "start_frame": 845,
      "end_frame": 891,
      "word_count": 5
    },
    {
      "text": "To rewrite the array, using those counts.",
      "start_ms": 30000,
      "end_ms": 33240,
      "start_frame": 900,
      "end_frame": 997,
      "word_count": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "So the problem is not the time complexity.",
      "start_ms": 34080,
      "end_ms": 36860,
      "start_frame": 1022,
      "end_frame": 1106,
      "word_count": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "O of n is already good.",
      "start_ms": 37640,
      "end_ms": 39560,
      "start_frame": 1129,
      "end_frame": 1187,
      "word_count": 6
    },
    {
      "text": "The limitation is, we first collect information, and only later place the values.",
      "start_ms": 40300,
      "end_ms": 45920,
      "start_frame": 1209,
      "end_frame": 1378,
      "word_count": 13
    },
    {
      "text": "Now think about this.",
      "start_ms": 46500,
      "end_ms": 47680,
      "start_frame": 1395,
      "end_frame": 1430,
      "word_count": 4
    },
    {
      "text": "Can we classify each value at the same moment we inspect it?",
      "start_ms": 48320,
      "end_ms": 52940,
      "start_frame": 1450,
      "end_frame": 1588,
      "word_count": 12
    },
    {
      "text": "Can zero move directly to the left, two move directly to the right, and one stay in the middle?",
      "start_ms": 52940,
      "end_ms": 61120,
      "start_frame": 1588,
      "end_frame": 1834,
      "word_count": 19
    },
    {
      "text": "If we can do that, we do not need a separate counting phase, and we do not need a separate rewrite phase.",
      "start_ms": 62060,
      "end_ms": 71480,
      "start_frame": 1862,
      "end_frame": 2144,
      "word_count": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "That is exactly where the three -pointer idea begins.",
      "start_ms": 72420,
      "end_ms": 76220,
      "start_frame": 2173,
      "end_frame": 2287,
      "word_count": 9
    }
  ],
